  "title": "At the knot's law, the knot's atom is a negation",
  "subject": "How a non-2-colourable cubic triple system minus one incidence acts as an edge gadget at each coupling",
  "conclusion": "A knot's space minus one incidence, placed on an edge, is an exact negation at the knot's law (lam = 0) and multiplies the paths through the edge by a ratio other than +-1 elsewhere (Fano: -141/6079 at lam = 1/2). At the dimer coupling lam = -3 every plain system counts (-2)^n times its perfect matchings, a determinant exactly on the knot's spaces.",
